"Vorg the Sapient" <spam@nospam.com> wrote:
[re mind flayers]
>I have no idea what's going on in the 2nd edition manual.

My guess at what happened is this: When they wrote second edition,
they realised that one of the big problems with 1st edition was that
psionics were drastically overpowered.  If you used the psionics rules,
it was possible to produce a first-level character who could arbitrarily
annihilate rooms full of non-psionic tenth-level characters.

Nobody had any stomach to try and rebalance the psionics then and there,
so they cut the psionics and made the illithids magical instead of
psionic.  When they subsequently released the "Complete Psionics
Handbook", they produced stats for illithids using the new psionics
rules.
